# Build context for api/, web/ and landing/ Dockerfiles is the repo root. Those
# Dockerfiles copy output that CI builds first (shared/dist, api/dist, web/.next,
# web/public, landing/out), so keep everything else out — a bloated context can
# wedge the Docker daemon on the shared VPS (see /opt/README.md there).
**/node_modules
.git
.github
.claude
infra
docs
scratch
test-results
api/reports
api/test
web/tests
**/coverage
web/.next/cache
landing/.next
*.docx

# Never bake local secrets into an image.
**/.env
**/.env.*
